[38;2;124;124;124mtheorem). Actually, more precisely: if $F$ is Lebesgue measurable on $\mathbb{R}[0m[38;2;124;124;124m^2$, then for almost every $y$, the function $x \mapsto F(x, y)$ is Lebesgue [0m
